.\" pragma: allowlist secret
.TH DEVID-ENROLL 1 "October 2026" "vtpm-mds" "User Commands" \" pragma: allowlist secret
.SH NAME
devid-enroll \- enroll or renew a guest LDevID via vtpm-mds \" pragma: allowlist secret
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B devid-enroll
.RB [ \-tpm
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-mds
.IR url ]
.RB [ \-out
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-cn
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-spire-data
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Guest helper that authenticates to
.B vtpm-mds \" pragma: allowlist secret
with MAC inventory identity and the TPM EK certificate, then writes SPIRE
.B tpm_devid
materials (PEM + TPM2B blobs).
.PP
On each run it renews when the certificate is missing, expired, or in the last
third of its validity; otherwise it exits successfully without calling enroll.
When renewing, an existing DevID key under
.I out
is reused when the blobs still load under the SPIRE H-1 storage parent.
.PP
When the certificate PEM bytes change and
.B \-spire-data
is set, the helper removes the SPIRE agent SVID cache
.RI ( agent-data.json
and related key material) under that directory and runs
.B systemctl try-restart spire-agent.service
so the next agent start attests the new LDevID. A missing or inactive
.B spire-agent
unit does not fail the renew.
.PP
The packaged oneshot runs
.B Before=spire-agent.service
(without
.BR Requires= )
and a daily timer repeats the check while the guest is up.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-tpm " path"
TPM device (default
.IR /dev/tpm0 ).
.TP
.BI \-mds " url"
MDS base URL (default
.IR http://169.254.169.254 ).
.TP
.BI \-out " dir"
Output directory (default
.IR /var/lib/vtpm-mds/devid ). \" pragma: allowlist secret
.TP
.BI \-cn " name"
Common Name to put into the platform identity of the signing request.
The service ignores it: the issued certificate's subject is always
.BI CN= vmid
and nothing else.
.TP
.BI \-spire-data " dir"
SPIRE agent
.BR data_dir .
On a PEM change the SVID cache under this directory is cleared and
.B spire-agent
is try-restarted. Empty disables both. Default
.IR /opt/spire/data/agent .
.TP
.B \-version
Print the package/build version and exit.
.SH SPIRE AGENT CLEANUP
Each renewed LDevID has a new SHA-1 fingerprint, so the SPIFFE agent ID under
.B tpm_devid
changes. Prefer registration selectors
.BI tpm_devid:subject:cn: vmid
over fingerprint paths. After renew, stale server entries can be removed with
SPIRE 1.14
.BR "spire-server agent evict" " (\-spiffeID)"
or
.BR "spire-server agent purge" " (\-expiredFor,"
default
.BR 720h ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vtpm-mds (8), \" pragma: allowlist secret
.BR systemctl (1)
